       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day, which is well above the usual limits:\n\n- **Daily maximum:** 4,000 mg/day for a healthy adult. Many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** The usual maximum is 1,000 mg. A 2,000 mg dose is double that.\n- **Risk:** Hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf 2000 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and give me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, but I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me which of the regimens above you want and I'll enter it."
