       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I asked for a clinical rationale and didn't get one. 6,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is about 1.5 times the maximum daily dose, and it carries a real risk of serious liver injury even in a patient with normal liver function. I don't know of any indication that calls for it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- 1000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day)\n- 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you have a specific reason for the higher dose, please talk to pharmacy first. Your institution's process for overriding dose limits would apply to the order. If you still want it entered after that, tell me what pharmacy approved. I can also add a note to the order, such as an approval reference or the rationale."
